      "writtenOn": "2021-02-04T19:01:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Confusingly, Soong uses tag (\":name{.tag}\") and deptag. This is a tag to specify which output path to use, similar to Bazel\u0027s implicit output targets (e.g. https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/java/app.go;l\u003d859-867;drc\u003d76b0852a481d3a0c81464e3470294e030b78c897). Updated the TODO here to specify what the tag looks like and better map it to a Bazel concept. The deptag allows connecting a dependency back to the requested use of that dependency.\n\nRight now, the deptag information is being ignored as we\u0027re mapping directly based on the items in the property. We could consider a mechanism to connect a property to a deptag if that gives us better granularity in the future.",
      "parentUuid": "8329c54a_2f560b54",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 431,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 431,
